  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-506696</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and five partners will implement Greening Our Rice: Gender-Just, Climate-Smart Rice Production (CSRP) in the Mekong Delta (GoRice), a CAD $8M initiative (2024-2030). The project aims to improve the well-being of rice producers, particularly women and ethnicminorities (EM), through inclusive and CSRP in the Mekong Delta, particularly Tra Vinh, An Giang, and Soc Trang provinces.
GoRice will promote climate-smart practices, enhance women&apos;s and ethnic minorities (EM) empowerment, support low-carbon (LC) rice consumption, and develop carbon Measurement, Reporting, and Verification (MRV) systems and fair carbon projects. GoRice will strengthen collaboration between stakeholders in Vietnam and Canada to enhance cost-benefit sharing mechanisms in carbon projects, green financing, investment, technology transfer, resource mobilization and policy frameworks supporting sustainable CSRP.
GoRice supports the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and Canada&#x2019;s Indo-Pacific Strategy (IPS), particularly objectives 3, 4, and 5. It aligns with Action Areas 1, 3, and 5 of the Feminist International Assistance Policy (FIAP), with a focus on Action Area 4, and incorporates relevant FIAP indicators into its Performance Measurement Framework (PMF). GoRice complies with the Official Development Assistance Accountability Act, the Comprehensive and Progressive Agreement for Trans-Pacific Partnership (CPTPP), and major international human rights commitments, including the ICCPR and ICESCR, to which Vietnam is a party. GoRice addresses gaps identified through gender equality, human rights, and environmental sustainability analyses, focusing on Article 23 of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights. By promoting sustainable agriculture (Chapter 20), decent work for women andvulnerable groups (Chapter 19), and inclusive economic growth (Chapter 21), GoRice contributes to the CPTPP&#x2019;s goals. GoRice will enhance trade and cooperation between Canada, Vietnam, and other CPTPP countries (Chapter 22), strengthening their reputationsin poverty reduction, gender equality, and environmental sustainability. Acomprehensive Communication and Visibility Action Plan will ensure stakeholder awareness of Canada&#x2019;s support through digital and print media, websites, social media, and campaigns.</narrative>
  </description>
